"}, {"@id": "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7160-3680", "@type": "Person", "familyName": "Hao", "givenName": "Bo", "name": "Hao, Bo"}, {"@id": "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2675-7290", "@type": "Person", "affiliation": [{"@type": "Organization", "name": "Janssen Research and Development Spring House"}], "familyName": "Aikonen", "givenName": "Santeri Alfred Arttu", "name": "Aikonen, Santeri Alfred Arttu"}, {"@id": "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-2922-6868", "@type": "Person", "familyName": "Diccianni", "givenName": "Justin", "name": "Diccianni, Justin"}, {"@id": "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1852-9434", "@type": "Person", "affiliation": [{"@type": "Organization", "name": "Johnson & Johnson Innovative Medicine"}], "familyName": "Wegner", "givenName": "J\u00f6rg Kurt", "name": "Wegner, J\u00f6rg Kurt"}, {"@id": "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3046-6576", "@type": "Person", "familyName": "Schwaller", "givenName": "Philippe", "name": "Schwaller, Philippe"}, {"@id": "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1502-5484", "@type": "Person", "familyName": "Strambeanu", "givenName": "Iulia", "name": "Strambeanu, Iulia"}], "dateCreated": "2026-04-17T22:17:11.792814+00:00", "dateModified": "2026-08-27T15:26:49.828940+00:00", "datePublished": "2026-04-18", "description": "<pre><br><br></pre>\n<p>This dataset contains ~27500 Buchwald Hartwig reactions, of which 11300 Buchwald&ndash;Hartwig reactions derived from a dedicated JnJ open-source data production effort in combination with a curated colection of 16200 open-source Buchwald&ndash;Hartwig / Pd-catalyzed C&ndash;N highthroughput experimentation reactions (see Dataset references below). Critically for generalization across sources, every chemical entity was curated with an internal JnJ tool to have a single consistent SMILES and Name representation across the entire combined set.</p>\n<div>If you use this dataset, please cite the associated publication: <strong>Neves, P. et al. &ldquo;Robust out-of-distribution prediction of Buchwald&ndash;Hartwig reactions.&rdquo;&nbsp;<em>Nature Computational Science</em>&nbsp;(2026).&nbsp;<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1038/s43588-026-01017-6\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://doi.org/10.1038/s43588-026-01017-6</a></strong></div>\n<p><br>Please also cite the original data sources where appropriate.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Santanilla, A. B. et al.&nbsp;<em>Nanomole-scale high-throughput chemistry for the synthesis of complex molecules.</em>&nbsp;<em>Science</em>,&nbsp;2015, 347, 49&ndash;53.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Ahneman, D. T.; Estrada, J. G.; Lin, S.; Dreher, S. D.; Doyle, A. G.<br><em>Predicting Reaction Performance in C&ndash;N Cross-Coupling Using Machine Learning.</em><br><em>Science</em>&nbsp;2018, 360, 186&ndash;190. DOI: 10.1126/science.aar5169.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Rinehart, N. I.; Saunthwal, R. K.; Wellauer, J.; Zahrt, A. F.; Schlemper, L.; Shved, A. S.; Bigler, R.; Fantasia, S.; Denmark, S. E.<br><em>A Machine-Learning Tool to Predict Substrate-Adaptive Conditions for Pd-Catalyzed C&ndash;N Couplings.</em><br><em>Science</em>&nbsp;2023, 381, 965&ndash;972.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Fitzner, M.; Wuitschik, G.; Koller, R. J.; Adam, J.-M.; Schindler, T.; Reymond, J.-L.<br><em>What Can Reaction Databases Teach Us about Buchwald&ndash;Hartwig Cross-Couplings?</em><br><em>Chem. Sci.</em>&nbsp;2020, 11, 13085&ndash;13093.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Saebi, M.; Nan, B.; Herr, J. E.; Bustillo, L.; Wiest, O.; Shields, B. J.; et al.<br><em>On the Use of Real-World Datasets for Reaction Yield Prediction.</em><br><em>Chem. Sci.</em>&nbsp;2023, 14, 1671&ndash;1685.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>King-Smith, E.; et al.<br><em>Probing the Chemical &ldquo;Reactome&rdquo; with High-Throughput Experimentation Data.</em><br><em>Nat. Chem.</em>&nbsp;2024, 16, 633&ndash;643.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Ha, S. K.; et al.<br><em>Developing Pharmaceutically Relevant Pd-Catalyzed C&ndash;N Coupling Reactivity Models Leveraging High-Throughput Experimentation.</em><br><em>J. Am. Chem. Soc.</em> 2025, 147, 19602&ndash;19613.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>", "distribution": [{"@type": "DataDownload", "contentUrl": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19636649/files/2026-02-21_df_HTE_BH_QM_10iter_9-3clustertest.pkl/content", "encodingFormat": "application/octet-stream"}], "identifier": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19636649", "license": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode", "name": "Collection of Curated Buchwald\u2013Hartwig HTE Reactions (2026-04-17)", "publisher": {"@type": "Organization", "name": "Zenodo"}, "size": "1.31 GB", "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/19636649", "volume": "6"}]}
